cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Atlas Physicus in research or teaching, please cite the software using this metadata."
title: "Atlas Physicus"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Tech Echo Collective"
version: "v3.0.5-alpha"
date-released: 2026-08-29
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tech-Echo-Collective/atlas-physicus"
url: "https://atlas.techecho.org/"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Atlas Physicus is an open scientific infrastructure prototype for exploring
  the geographic, temporal, and institutional structure of the global physics
  research ecosystem. Part of Tech Echo Physica, a Tech Echo Collective project
  family for exploring physics through research mapping, knowledge structures,
  and interactive physical systems. Earlier names were Physics Atlas and Atlas
  Physica; historical releases retain their original names and identifiers.
keywords:
  - physics
  - scientific infrastructure
  - research ecosystem
  - geographic visualization
  - open science
